                <pb facs="0463" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg378"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/1890: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-19T11:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">July 19,
                                1919</hi>, [<hi rendition="#italic">11 a.m.</hi>]</date><lb/>[<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received July 20, 11.16
                    a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Believed to be in peril of life and limb, General Saturnino Medal has taken
                    refuge temporarily in the Legation. No demand has been made on me for release by
                    the Government. Most prominent men under political charge brutally treated and
                    placed in penitentiary and I believe lives in peril. Please advise me definitely
                    in the premises immediately after enciphering [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>]
                    the above. Silverio Lainez, Lopez Padilla and Colonel Raimundo Valladares [also
                    given refuge].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
